    "durationMs": 119165,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/main.py` — FastAPI app with all four endpoints: `POST /links` (201, generated or custom codes, 409 on duplicate), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`), `GET /links/{code}`, and `GET /r/{code}` (302 with atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` click increment)\n- `app/models.py` + Alembic migration — `links` table in PostgreSQL, credentials read from `DATABASE_URL` (converted to the `postgresql+psycopg://` driver form)\n- Error handlers normalize all failures to JSON with an `error` field: 409/404 via `HTTPException`, and a `RequestValidationError` handler covering malformed JSON, missing/invalid `url`, and invalid `code` as 422\n- `start.sh` — runs `alembic upgrade head`, then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (no installs inside)\n- `README.md` with the start instructions; `requirements.txt` pins the stack dependencies (no extras needed)\n\n**Verification results:** every endpoint tested with curl — URLs returned byte-identical (no pydantic `HttpUrl` normalization), code boundaries (4 and 20 chars) accepted, 15 generated codes all unique, redirects increment clicks exactly once per request, and after a full server restart the data and click counts persisted with migrations running idempotently. Test server has been stopped, so port 8000 is free."
  }
